# file-toto — Project Overview

## What This Project Is

`file-toto` is a faithful CLI replica of the Unix `file` command (the classic
type-classification utility; not a GNU coreutils binary). For each path
operand it prints a short description of what the file appears to be — using
filesystem metadata, then embedded magic signatures on a content prefix, then
simple text/binary heuristics.

Output is one result line per operand on stdout. There is **no** infinite
output loop and **no** external magic database / libmagic dependency.

## Binary Name

The compiled binary must always be named **`file-toto`**. Never rename it.
On Windows, MinGW may also emit `file-toto.exe`; that is the same program.

## Platforms

| Platform | Build environment | Notes |
|----------|-------------------|-------|
| **Linux** | `gcc`/`clang` + GNU Make | Full POSIX path: `lstat`/`stat`, `open`/`read` |
| **Windows** | **MSYS2 UCRT64** (recommended) | Native Windows `.exe`; binary-mode opens; symlink support as available under MinGW |
| **Git Bash** | Works if `/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is **early** on `PATH` | Same binary as UCRT64; see `toolchain-structure.mdc` |

Binaries are **not portable** across OSes — build separately on Linux and on
Windows.

## Scope — Keep It Minimal

Supporting behaviour:

- Built-in `--help` / `--h` and `--version` / `--v` (detected anywhere in
  `argv`; help wins if both appear)
- `-b` / `--brief`, `-i` / `--mime` / `--mime-type`, `-h` / `--no-dereference`,
  `-L` / `--dereference`, `-E` (fatal filesystem errors)
- Compiled-in magic for common formats + empty / directory / symlink / text /
  data fallbacks

**Do not add**:

- Interactive or TUI modes
- External magic files (`-m` / `--magic-file`) or libmagic
- Compression walking (`-z`), apple, extension, or sandbox flags
- Logging or debug output in normal operation
- Single-dash `-v` as version (version is `--version` / `--v` only; `-v` is
  reserved / unused — do not invent GNU `file -v` unless requested)
- Any feature that would break Unix `file` behavioural compatibility for the
  supported subset

## Behavioural Contract

| Invocation | Output / behaviour |
|---|---|
| `file-toto file.txt` | `file.txt: ASCII text` (or similar human description) |
| `file-toto a.png b.pdf` | one `name: type` line per operand, in order |
| `file-toto -b file.txt` | description only (no `filename: ` prefix) |
| `file-toto -i file.txt` | MIME type (e.g. `file.txt: text/plain`) |
| `file-toto -h link` | classify the symlink itself |
| `file-toto -L link` | follow symlink; classify the target |
| `file-toto missing` | stdout result line about cannot open; exit `0` |
| `file-toto -E missing` | stderr diagnostic; exit `1` |
| `file-toto --version` / `file-toto --v` | `file-toto <version>\n`, exit `0` |
| `file-toto --help` / `file-toto --h` | usage on stdout, exit `0` |

At least one file operand is required (after flags).

## Exit Codes

| Code | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `0` | Classification completed; `--help`; `--version`; cannot-open **without** `-E` |
| `1` | Bad option, write failure, or filesystem errors when `-E` is set |

